    "custom_comments": "CFM: Jane Doe 04/26\nPest Control: Cornerstone 10/26\n\nObservations: \nWalk in refrigerator 40F\nPrep Table 38F\n\nViolations:\n#9. Observed raw chicken over raw eggs. Separate according to cook temperature. Food must be separated and protected to limit contamination.\n#18. Observed Spray bottle without label. Label. Poisonous/toxic materials or chemicals must be labeled with the common name of the substance.\n#32. Observed wiping cloth stored under cutting boards. Remove and obtain anti-slip cutting mat. Food contact surfaces must be smooth, durable, and cleanable.\n#36. Observed wiping cloth improperly stored. Remove. Wiping clothes must be properly laundered or stored in sanitizer solution in between uses.\n#37. Observed food item being stored on the floor. Remove. Food must be stored at least 6 inches above the floor.\n#42. A) Observed accumulation throughout the establishment on vents, floors, drains, and etc. Clean. Nonfood-contact surfaces of equipment shall be kept free of an accumulation of dust, dirt, food residue, and other debris.\n\tB) Observed rust on air vents. Remove/Repair/Replace. Nonfood-contact surfaces of equipment that are exposed to splash, spillage, or other food soiling or that require frequent cleaning shall be constructed of a corrosion-resistant, nonabsorbent, and smooth material and shall be kept free of an accumulation of dust, dirt, food residue, and other debris.\n#45. Observed damaged floor tiles. Repair/Replace. The physical facilities shall be maintained in good repair.\n#47. Observed residential freezer. Remove. Only Commercial/NSF equipment is allowed in the establishment.\n\nComments:",
