    "custom_comments": "CFM: Jane Doe 11/29\nPest Control: Contail 10/26\n\nTemperatures:\nWalk in refrigerator 38F\nPrep Table 39\nHot Holding\n\tChicken 154\n\tBeef 160\n\nViolations:\n#6. Observed eggs and sushi rice without written time procedure. If temperature is not being used as an control then time is to be used as a control and a written procedure shall be prepared in advance, maintained in the establishment\n#10. Observed soil build up in ice machine. Food contact surfaces must be cleaned, sanitized and in good repair.\n#28. Observed food without date labeled in the multiple in refrigerator. Label. TCS/RTE Foods that are prepared and in the establishment over 24hrs must be properly marked with the common name and prep date and must be consumed or discarded within 7 days of being prepared or opened by a food establishment.\n#31. Observed handwashing sink inaccessible. Remove. Handwashing facilities must be accessible at all times for employee use and may not be used for purposes other than hand washing.\n#32. A) Observed cardboard/wood on shelving. Remove. All surfaces must be smooth, durable, and cleanable.\n\tB) Observed damaged cooking kitchen equipment. Remove/Replace. All food contact surfaces may not allow the migration of substances.\n\tC) Observed food being stored on paper towel. Remove. Food items must only be in contact with an approved food contact surfaces. \n\tD) Observed rust on magnetic knife holder. Remove/Replace. All food contact surfaces may not allow the migration of substances.\n\tE) Observed protective plastic on Equipment. Remove.\n#36. Observed wiping cloth improperly stored. Remove. Wiping clothes must be properly laundered or stored in sanitizer solution in between uses.\n#37. A) Observed food item being stored on the floor. Remove. Food must be stored at least 6 inches above the floor.\n\tB) Observed food unprotected throughout establishment. Protect. Food protected from cross contamination by storing the food in packages, covered containers, or wrapping.\n#39. A) Observed plates stored unprotected. Clean equipment and utensils must be properly stored as specified under paragraph of this subsection and shall be stored covered or inverted.\n\tB) Observed damaged gaskets on hot box in kitchen. Replace \n\tC) Observed dispensing utensils in warm water. Remove. During pauses in food preparation or dispensing, food preparation and dispensing utensils shall be stored in a container of water if the water is maintained at a temperature of at least 135 degrees Fahrenheit) and the container is cleaned at a frequency specified under \u00a7228.114(a)(4)(G) of this title.\n#41. Observed bulk container without labels. Label. All containers must be labeled with common name.\n#42. Observed accumulation throughout the establishment on vents, floors, drains, and etc. Clean. Nonfood-contact surfaces of equipment shall be kept free of an accumulation of dust, dirt, food residue, and other debris.\n#43. Observed dirty and damaged vent hoods. Clean/Repair. Ventilation hood systems shall be adequate and cleaned so they are not a source of contamination by dust, dirt, and other materials.\n#45. Observed damaged grout throughout establishment. Repair. Ensure grout is level with floor tile. The physical facilities shall be maintained in good repair.\n\nComments:\n- Observed Spray bottle without label. Label. Poisonous/toxic materials or chemicals must be labeled with the common name of the substance.",
